  "name": "luh-calibrations-accurauto",
  "notes": "This zip package contains multi-GNSS vehicle antenna calibration results generated within the __ACCURAUTO__ project (Accurate prediction of GNSS antenna performance in automotive scenarios). All results are provided in the ANTEX (Antenna Exchange) format and include:\r\n\r\n-   Phase center offsets and variations (PCO/PCV) per frequency block (entries under _START OF FREQUENCY_)\r\n-  Group delay variations for code measurements (GDV, also referred to as code‑phase center corrections, CPC; entries under _START OF GDV_)\r\n\r\n\r\nThe archive is organized into two top-level folders with results from DLR and Geopp:\r\n\r\n-  DLR: ANTEX files for multiple vehicle orientations relative to the calibration setup, including runs that incorporate the vehicle CAD model, as well as standalone antenna calibrations.\r\n-  Geopp: calibration results for the standalone antenna (folder \"Roboter\") and for the antenna mounted on the vehicle (folder \"Insitu\").\r\n\r\n\r\nFurther details on __ACCURAUTO__ are available in:\r\n\r\n-  Kröger, J., Ren, L., Wübbena, J., Tripathi, V., Caizzone, S., and Schön, S. (2024). _Impact of GNSS receivers on GNSS antenna performance prediction for automotive scenarios_. In: 11th ESA Workshop on Satellite Navigation Technologies and European Workshop on GNSS Signals and Signal Processing (NAVITEC), Noordwijk, The Netherlands. Presentation\r\n-  Tripathi, Veenu and Caizzone, Stefano (2025). _Hybrid GNSS Antenna Characterization for Automotive Scenarios_. European Conference on Antennas and Propagation (EuCAP) 2025, 2025-03-30 - 2025-04-04, Stockholm, Sweden",
